          "body": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<title>Portland extends its bike-lane network to the eastern suburbs — The Ledger</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"The council approved 41 kilometres of protected lane, most of it east of 82nd Avenue.\">\n<meta name=\"author\" content=\"Marion Delacroix\">\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2026-07-28T06:00:00-07:00\">\n<meta property=\"article:modified_time\" content=\"2026-07-30T14:12:00-07:00\">\n<meta property=\"article:section\" content=\"Transport\">\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://the-ledger.example/transport/portland-bike-lane-network-east\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"application/rss+xml\" title=\"The Ledger — Transport\" href=\"/feeds/transport.xml\">\n<script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"NewsArticle\",\"headline\":\"Portland extends its bike-lane network to the eastern suburbs\",\"description\":\"The council approved 41 kilometres of protected lane, most of it east of 82nd Avenue.\",\"author\":{\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\":\"Marion Delacroix\"},\"publisher\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"The Ledger\"},\"datePublished\":\"2026-07-28T06:00:00-07:00\",\"dateModified\":\"2026-07-30T14:12:00-07:00\",\"articleSection\":\"Transport\",\"isAccessibleForFree\":false,\"hasPart\":{\"@type\":\"WebPageElement\",\"isAccessibleForFree\":false,\"cssSelector\":\".paywalled-body\"}}</script>\n</head>\n<body>\n<header><nav><a href=\"/\">Home</a> <a href=\"/transport\">Transport</a> <a href=\"/city-hall\">City Hall</a></nav></header>\n<main>\n<article>\n<h1>Portland extends its bike-lane network to the eastern suburbs</h1>\n<p class=\"byline\">By Marion Delacroix · 28 July 2026</p>\n<p>The council approved 41 kilometres of protected lane on Tuesday evening, most of it east of 82nd Avenue, in the largest single expansion of the network since 2019.</p>\n<p>The vote was 4–1. The lanes will be built in three phases between spring 2027 and the end of 2029, and the transport bureau has already scheduled the first design workshops for the Montavilla and Powellhurst-Gilbert segments.</p>\n<div class=\"paywalled-body\">\n<p>Council members had spent most of the afternoon on the question of parking removal on Division Street, where the plan converts…</p>\n<p class=\"wall\">This article is for subscribers. <a href=\"/subscribe\">Subscribe</a> to read the rest.</p>\n</div>\n</article>\n</main>\n<footer><p>© 2026 The Ledger. Portland, Oregon.</p></footer>\n</body>\n</html>\n",
